          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Angiosperms — Efficient reproduction and seed dispersal"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.11,
            0.69,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Angiosperms (angeion means vessel and spermos means seeds) or flowering plants, represent plants with the most complex body organisation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.704,
            0.117,
            0.765,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 6 Curiosity Chapter 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.164,
            0.776,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "They produce flowers and fruits (Fig. 12.13). Flowers attract pollinators, increasing the efficiency of reproduction, while fruits help spread seeds to new locations. These features allow angiosperms to occupy a wide range of environments. Therefore, they are the most diverse plant group on the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
